      "lineNbr": 219,
      "author": {
        "id": 1139038
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-31T11:00:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This means there\u0027s a standard header for each partition, which is a good thing but is it well defined what is standard and what is partitions specific? Or would that be left to what\u0027s inside the partition?\n\nIf the latter, then I think we want a version somewhere e.g. if microdroid wanted to change its algorithm (e.g. just sign without encrypting) or similar. That could be inside the partition of an extra field in this header.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b72dc922a0cef58651be2ddaa161f3266969cd55",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f6d19c09_be4c1ddf",
        "filename": "microdroid_manager/src/instance.rs",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 219,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-31T13:43:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The format of the header is not specific to each partition. It\u0027s just (UUID, size). The version number in the disk header defines the format of all partition headers on the disk.\n\nPartition-specific format is limited to the payload. The data format shall define its own version field. That version shall not be shown in the partition header, because that information is useless to other users of the instance disk.\n\nA change like stopping the encryption could (and I think should) be handled by migrating to (or forking) another UUID. There really is no ordering (or compatible conversions) between the different formats. They are just completely different formats that need to be handled separately.",
      "parentUuid": "95d23cdc_9c398d0c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 219,
        "startChar": 30,
        "endLine": 219,
        "endChar": 44
      },
      "revId": "b72dc922a0cef58651be2ddaa161f3266969cd55",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
